\subsection{Making the Backend Independent from QGIS}

Some backend methods still depended on QGIS.  
To enable a fully independent hydrological twin, these dependencies were removed and replaced with pure Python and GeoPandas implementations.

\begin{itemize}
    \item Created \texttt{interface/GeoDataProvider.py}
    \item Modified \texttt{interface/ExploreData.py}
    \item Modified \texttt{backend/Compartment.py}
    \item Modified \texttt{backend/Mesh.py}
    \item Modified \texttt{backend/Extraction.py}
    \item Modified \texttt{backend/Observations.py}
    \item Created \texttt{backend/tools/spatial\_utils.py}
\end{itemize}

Two new files were introduced:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \texttt{GeoDataProvider}: fetches geodata from either QGIS layers or shapefiles.
    \item \texttt{spatial\_utils}: replacement for \texttt{GisLayerManager}, providing shared spatial utilities.
\end{itemize}

Frontend systems handling backend data (e.g.\ \texttt{DialogSpatialMaps}) were updated accordingly.

